Evidence:
  - Spring Cloud Documentation
  - Kubernetes Documentation
  - Production experience

Rules:
  [J1] Use Spring Cloud for service discovery and configuration.
  [J2] Use Resilience4j for circuit breaking and rate limiting.
  [J3] Use Spring Cloud Gateway for API gateway.
  [J4] Implement distributed tracing with Micrometer Tracing.
  [J5] Use Kubernetes for deployment and scaling.
  [J6] Implement health checks with Spring Boot Actuator.
  [J7] Use message brokers (Kafka/RabbitMQ) for async communication.
  [J8] Implement graceful shutdown with shutdown hooks.

Pros:
  - Scalable architecture
  - Independent deployment
  - Enterprise ecosystem

Cons:
  - Operational complexity
  - Memory footprint
  - Network latency

Alternatives:
  - Quarkus (lower memory)
  - Go (simpler concurrency)

State: +

